  "notes": [
    "The same modal and hook save both new and existing indexers: id 0 -> POST /indexer (CreateProvider), id > 0 -> PUT /indexer/{id} (UpdateProvider). Frontend apiRoot is /api/v5, so the V5 controllers are followed; V3 has parallel controllers.",
    "Frontend skip rules in saveProvider (useProviderSettings.ts): 'if (provider.id > 0 && !hasChangedValues && !hasChangedFields) {' sends skipTesting and skipValidation=all; 'if (isResave) {' sends skipTesting; 'if (errors.length === 0 && warnings.length > 0) {' sends skipValidation=warnings.",
    "ValidateResource runs in RestController.OnActionExecuting before the action (not a step). VerifyValidationResult is reached from GetDefinition (Validate) and from Test.",
    "Settings validators vary per indexer implementation (Newznab, Torznab, FileList, HDBits, IPTorrents, Nyaa, Torrentleech, TorrentRss, BroadcastheNet, Fanzub); only Newznab rules are listed under checks.",
    "Test(failures) is implemented per indexer type; HttpIndexerBase.TestConnection's FetchPage is the outside HTTP request, not walked (depth).",
    "Not followed: V3 IndexerController; HealthCheck [CheckOn] consumers are listed as message links by name.",
    "Step 2 -> 3: save() is a useCallback wrapping mutate (useProviderSettings.ts:131-135), not walked as its own step."
  ]
}